---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import siteConfig from '@/site-config'
import TypedText from '@/components/TypedText.vue'

const funFacts = [
  '🔧 X++ by day, Go by night',
  '🖥️ one flake, three machines, no manual setup',
  '📷 photography: ordinary places, good light',
  '♟️ cp-archives: competitive programming in C++ and Go',
]
---

<BaseLayout description={siteConfig.description}>
  <article class="prose lg:prose-xl">
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      Greetings! My name is
      <b>Hidayat Taufiqur</b>
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-md">
      <TypedText
        client:load
        messages={funFacts}
        type-speed={55}
        delete-speed={28}
        pause-time={1500}
        between-pause={2000}
        aria-label="Fun facts about me"
      />
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      My route here was not the tidy one. An apprenticeship in February 2023, an internship at <b>Telkom Indonesia</b>
      that September, a year of freelance work from March 2024, then a full time role at <b>9 Dots Consulting</b> in March
      2025, a few months after graduation. Four arrangements in two years, each one a codebase I had to learn while real users
      already depended on it. That is a faster education than a stable first job would have been, and a lot less comfortable.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      I started at <b>Telkom University</b> in 2020 and finished in 2024 with an <b>S.Kom. in Informatics</b>, GPA 3.76,
      <b>Cum Laude</b>. The transcript is the least interesting thing about those four years. I was a practicum
      assistant for over <b>250 students</b>, teaching data structures to people who were completely lost. Explaining a
      linked list to someone who does not see it yet is a stricter test of understanding than any exam. Then
      <b>Proclub</b>, the campus tech club, first as lead software engineer and later as president. The Teknofest
      registration portal we built there carried more than a thousand participants. For my thesis I measured HTTP
      versions against backend application performance, which is how I ended up reading protocol documentation for fun.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      Telkom Indonesia is where I ran into a system too big to hold in my head. I came in through the DBT program in
      early 2023 and stayed on as a backend intern, working on a <b>MySQL to SingleStore</b> migration with a team of eight.
      Queries got meaningfully faster once the data lived where the workload wanted it. The service itself was Go, split along
      domain boundaries with CQRS and microservices, with a Camunda process API holding the workflows together. Eight people,
      one architecture, and a lot of arguing about where each boundary belongs. That was the part school never taught.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      The freelance year had one project worth naming. <b>Nusantara Food Ontology</b> needed competency questions for a domain
      ontology, the kind of expert-heavy writing nobody enjoys. I built a Flask backend that drafts them with LangChain, OpenAI,
      and retrieval over the source material. Generation came out about <b>1.5× faster</b>, and the path from a code
      change to production got roughly <b>3× faster</b> once GitHub Actions was doing the deploying. The point was never the
      speed figure. It was an expert spending the hours on ontology design instead of typing questions into a document.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      9 Dots Consulting then handed me D365FO, an ERP I had never opened, and a team patient enough to let me read the
      code until it made sense. A year and a half in production later the part I enjoy most is still the part I was
      worst at on day one. Most of the work is reading the standard application until you find where a process actually
      breaks. My favourite hunt so far was a Power BI refresh that kept hitting the timeout. Nothing in the report
      pointed anywhere useful. The cause was an unused tax-calculation side effect buried inside the standard
      exchange-rate call, quietly costing time the whole while. A system never lies to you. It is just answering a
      question you did not ask.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      Not every problem is that interesting. The boring ones are usually the ones people notice. A client was keying
      sales orders by hand, all day, off spreadsheets. We replaced it with an import that takes five Excel templates,
      validates everything in staging, then creates the orders and lines with optional auto-invoicing. The code was the
      easy part. What stays with me is a room of people who stopped retyping the same numbers and got their time back.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      On my own time I keep building things nobody asked for. This site and a couple of services run on a VPS I
      configure declaratively, sharing one flake with my laptop and desktop. I write in Neovim, which is a decision that
      needs explaining to almost everyone. The largest side project is FnO Navigator, a map of the D365FO table graph,
      built because the database is thousands of tables deep and Microsoft does not ship a compass. There is also a
      public archive of competitive programming solutions in C++ and Go.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-lg">
      The rest of my time goes to a guitar I have owned for years and still cannot play properly, Chelsea matches I
      refuse to miss even at 3am, Valorant with friends when everyone is online, and a Mobile Legends jungle I treat
      with a seriousness the game does not deserve.
    </p>

    <div class="not-prose mt-10">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">Experience</h3>
      <dl class="space-y-2 text-sm text-main">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">9 Dots Consulting</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">Associate Technical Developer · 2025–present</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Nusantara Food Ontology</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">Backend Developer (Freelance) · 2024–2025</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Telkom Indonesia</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">Backend Developer Intern · 2023–2024</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Telkom Indonesia</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">Backend Stream (DBT Program) · 2023</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Informatics Laboratory</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">Practicum Assistant · 2022–2023</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Proclub Telkom University</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">President (2023–2024) · Lead Software Engineer (2022–2023)</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-8">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">Education</h3>
      <dl class="space-y-1 text-sm text-main">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="shrink-0 w-48 font-semibold">Telkom University</dt>
          <dd class="opacity-70">S.Kom. Informatics · GPA 3.76/4.00 Cum Laude · 2020–2024</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-8">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-3">Toolbox</h3>
      <dl class="space-y-2 text-sm text-main">
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Languages</dt>
          <dd>TypeScript, JavaScript, Go, Python, Java, C/C++, Bash, X++</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Frameworks</dt>
          <dd>Node.js, Express, Laravel, Flask, React, React Native, LangChain</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Databases</dt>
          <dd>PostgreSQL, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, MongoDB, Redis</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Cloud &amp; DevOps</dt>
          <dd>
            GCP, Hyperledger Fabric, Docker, <a
              href="https://github.com/hidayattaufiqur/nix-config"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="prose-link">Nix</a
            >, GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Monitoring &amp; Servers</dt>
          <dd>Prometheus, Grafana, Nginx</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-2">
          <dt class="font-semibold shrink-0 w-40">Specialized</dt>
          <dd>
            D365FO, SSRS, LCS, Linux, <a
              href="https://github.com/hidayattaufiqur/cracked.nvchad"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="prose-link">Neovim</a
            >, Postman, Notion, AI/Agents
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">Photography</h3>
      <p class="text-lg">
        I take photographs of ordinary places and the light that happens to be falling on them. A selection lives
        <a href="/photography" aria-label="See my photography gallery" class="prose-link">here</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-lg mt-6">
      The full timeline is in my
      <b><a href="/resume.pdf" target="_blank" aria-label="View my CV/resume" class="prose-link">CV/resume</a></b>.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <p class="text-lg">Elsewhere on the internet:</p>
      <div class="flex gap-x-4 gap-y-2 flex-wrap mt-4">
        {
          siteConfig.socialLinks.map((link) => (
            <a
              aria-label={link.text}
              href={link.href}
              target="_blank"
              class="prose-link text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors duration-200 flex items-center p-2 rounded hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-gray-700"
            >
              <i class:list={[link.icon]} class="text-xl mr-2" />
              {link.text}
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
        Email me at
        <a
          class="text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-700 transition-colors duration-200"
          aria-label={siteConfig.email}
          href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}
        >
          {siteConfig.email}
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
